message: >-
  If you use EnCoDaPy in your work, please cite the Zenodo release and this
  software package.
title: 'EnCoDaPy - Energy Control and Data Preparation in Python'
type: software
version: 0.9.2
date-released: '2026-07-02'
repository-code: https://github.com/gewv-tu-dresden/encodapy
url: https://gewv-tu-dresden.github.io/encodapy/
license: BSD-3-Clause
abstract: >-
  EnCoDaPy (Energy Control and Data Preparation in Python) is a modular Python
  framework designed for the real-time management and optimisation of
  decentralised energy systems. Its modular and extensible architecture offers
  flexibility, facilitating the development, validation and operation of
  control strategies for energy systems.

  Key features:

  - Configuration management: Structured models for system and component
    configurations.
  - Data integration: Support for various interfaces, including MQTT, FIWARE
    and file-based systems.
  - Component control: Modular architecture for managing energy system
    components.
  - Data validation: Robust data processing using Pydantic-based models.

  EnCoDaPy is open source and is designed for researchers, engineers and
  practitioners specialising in energy system modelling and optimisation.
keywords:
  - energy systems
  - sector coupling
  - data analysis
  - control
  - optimization
  - FIWARE
  - MQTT
  - Python
  - Pydantic
